+(defcustom markdown-ts-percent-decode-destinations t
+  "Non-nil means percent-decode a local link destination before opening it.
+CommonMark takes a link destination as written: `my%20file.md' names
+exactly that, and only reading the destination as a URI reference makes
+it name `my file.md'.  Many Markdown tools write local paths
+percent-encoded all the same -- Obsidian does -- so this is on by
+default.
+
+Set it to nil if one of your file names contains a literal `%' followed
+by two hexadecimal digits, which decoding would misread.
+
+This option does not affect CommonMark's `<...>' destination wrapper.
+Those brackets are syntax rather than part of the destination, and are
+always removed."
+  :type 'boolean
+  :safe #'booleanp
+  :version "32.1"
   :package-version "1.0")
 
